course: dictionary
lesson: 10232
title: Toe in context
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A toe is one of the five parts at the end of your foot. The same word can also be part of a phrase, and the words around it show you which meaning is meant. In «Geckos stick to glass with millions of tiny toe hairs», the hairs are on the parts at the ends of the gecko's feet, so toe means a part of a foot.
explain: «But if your toe touches the three-point line, it's only a 2.» Here toe is the tip of a foot touching a line on a court, and the words three-point line tell you the game is basketball. Try your meaning in the sentence: "if your foot touches the line" still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Phrases use toe in a special way. «He is always on his toes» means he is alert and ready. «She won't toe the line» means she will not obey the rules, and «tread on someone's toes» means to upset them. When a phrase seems strange, ask what the whole phrase is trying to say.
fact: A toe is one of the five parts at the end of your foot, like fingers on your hand.
fact: The toe of a shoe or sock is the part that covers your toes.
fact: Animals have toes too: they are the parts at the ends of their feet.
fact: «Tiptoe» means to walk quietly on the front of your feet and toes.
fact: Phrases: «on your toes» means alert; «toe the line» means obey the rules; «tread on someone's toes» means upset someone.
exercise: «Geckos stick to glass with millions of tiny toe hairs.» Which part of a gecko has the hairs? | Its tail | Its eyes | *Its toes | Its ears
exercise: In the phrase «on your toes», what does it mean? | Wearing new socks | Very tired | Standing on tiptoe | *Alert and ready
exercise: What is the toe of a shoe? | *The part that covers your toes | The laces that tie the shoe | The heel at the back | The thick sole under the foot
test: What does «toe the line» mean? | Run very fast | Stand very still | Lose a race | *Obey the rules
test: What does «tread on someone's toes» mean? | Walk on the grass | Paint their feet | Hug them | *Upset them
exam: What does «tiptoe» mean? | Jump high | *Walk quietly on the front of your feet | Kick a ball hard | Run very fast
